{"id": "EUVD-2026-83255", "enisaUuid": "45ca97aa-2fc3-3612-8d83-8ae66ee3190b", "description": "http-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 contains a cache validation vulnerability in the _varyMatches() function that fails to properly validate Vary header wildcards due to byte-for-byte string comparison. Attackers can request URLs previously fetched by other clients to receive cached responses intended for different users, disclosing sensitive information across clients.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T17:51:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:23:09", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/kornelski/http-cache-semantics/issues/57", "https://github.com/kornelski/http-cache-semantics", "https://github.com/kornelski/http-cache-semantics/blob/f01112e954b83cfa8765b633ba880e5e980aa54c/index.js#L483-L501", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/http-cache-semantics-through-4.2.0-cross-client-cache-disclosure-via-vary-wildcard"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93750", "GHSA-f27v-pv5m-c5g6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7875ac11-a0f9-37b7-8345-f840da4f8741", "product": {"name": "http-cache-semantics", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c54b1a53-9d83-3263-a824-9b62eb18da63", "vendor": {"name": "kornelski"}}], "isExploited": false}